    "faq": {
      "type": "thg-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's included?",
            "answer": "<p>Four days of instruction from 8 pro instructors, classroom and field sessions, lodging in heated log cabins, family-style meals, and The Hunter's Gathering field kit (over $400 value).</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the payment plan work, and when is the balance due?",
            "answer": "<p>Reserve with a $350 deposit today. The remaining $1,445 is split into 3 automatic payments of $481.67, with the final payment due March 15, 2027. You can also pay the full $1,795 at checkout.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's your cancellation, refund and transfer policy?",
            "answer": "<p>Your seat is transferable to another hunter at any time. Deposits are non-refundable. If you must cancel your registration we will carry the deposit forward toward the year's gathering.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the cabins and lodging like?",
            "answer": "<p>You'll stay in heated log cabins at Cascades Camp & Conference Center in Yelm, WA. . Each cabin accommodates 6-11 guests in generous, twin-sized bunks, and one twin/queen bunk. Each cabin has a private bath and shower. Bring bedding and towels.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need to be an experienced hunter?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Sessions are built for both new and seasoned hunters. Whether you're filling your first tag or chasing a record-class animal, you'll leave with tactics you can use this season.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What should I bring?",
            "answer": "<p>Casual clothing for classes and hiking clothes, and shoes &nbsp;for our field sessions</p><p>We also recommend you bring some mosquito and tick repellent with you.</p><p>Camp chairs for campfires.</p><p><strong>Bring your own sleeping bag, pillow, towels (including hand towels), and toiletries.</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong>If you are flying in, let us know - we can assist with bedding.</strong></span></p><p>The full list will also be in the 2027 Event Guide.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I'm flying in. What's the nearest airport?",
            "answer": "<p>Seattle-Tacoma International (SEA) is about one hour away. Portland International (PDX) is about two hours away. [Confirm with Asha] Add whether shuttle or carpool options are available.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I come by myself?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely. Many hunters come solo and leave with mentors, hunting partners and lifelong friends. Meals, campfires and shared cabins make it easy to meet people.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can my spouse, kids or partner attend?",
            "answer": "<p>Family groups save $100 with a code at checkout. Minors must attend with a guardian and be at least 12 years of age to participate.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
